  "description": "Every refusal code the snapshot bridge emits, with the scope the route gives it. A capture-scoped refusal speaks for one capture and keeps the app generation on the bridge; generation-scoped codes retire the generation, and runner-session-scoped codes retire the runner bridge. Emitters: the Objective-C reader (apple/snapshot-bridge), the runner-served bridge (RunnerSnapshotBridge.m, RunnerTests+SnapshotBridge.swift), and the TypeScript snapshot source (packages/platform-apple/src/snapshot-source, runner-snapshot-bridge.ts). The TypeScript policy packages/platform-apple/src/snapshot-route-failure-policy.ts mirrors this table. test/repo-guards/snapshot-bridge-refusals.test.ts fails when an emitted code is missing here, when a code here is emitted nowhere, or when the policy disagrees. Classify a new code here by an explicit decision; an unlisted code fails the guard.",
